# Pinned host keys for the hosts named in configs/ssh/config, read through
# UserKnownHostsFile alongside the regular known_hosts. A named host that
# presents a different key is refused even on a fresh machine, where
# StrictHostKeyChecking accept-new would otherwise trust whatever answers
# first. Public data. When a host is legitimately reinstalled, replace its
# lines here (ssh-keyscan <host>) and commit; tests/test_ssh.zsh requires an
# ed25519 entry for every named host.
# vm is the UTM guest, reached by the mDNS name it announces.
vm-aarch64.local ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJEbcBngKg6l/zHOmGBhc513akyxDvyd0NDZqKpe1kXb
vm-aarch64.local ssh-rsa 
192.168.1.178 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIM2t90KGNlOq3AechfUmFc8FUhFAwkSc0f4RJSVi2pf5
192.168.1.178 ssh-rsa 
# wintermute over the tailnet (configs/ssh/config). From a peer, Tailscale
# SSH answers port 22 with its own ecdsa key (/var/lib/tailscale/ssh on the
# box); sshd's ed25519 key is what answers when Tailscale SSH is off.
wintermute.risk-basking.ts.net,100.67.58.61 ecdsa-sha2-nistp256 AAAAE2VjZHNhLXNoYTItbmlzdHAyNTYAAAAIbmlzdHAyNTYAAABBBCLBYGSViq7UKHYjJ/0ivOfm4fympLTc41O646RJmZOx2QGM6Mo3/mEwbyokdnbJ6aLnwV5EoJCt6rS0AHndtlM=
wintermute.risk-basking.ts.net,100.67.58.61 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIM2t90KGNlOq3AechfUmFc8FUhFAwkSc0f4RJSVi2pf5
10.10.2.90 ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIJrsiIGctj5tBCnoFTtT5wwQ6RxzFVH2rbe9qdQj2k4M
10.10.2.90 ssh-rsa 
